James encountered an issue with the `pickerInput` in his Shiny app, where it wouldn't open despite showing the default value. I provided a systematic triage approach, listing potential causes such as missing JavaScript/CSS, version mismatches, CSS/JS conflicts, or UI creation timing. I suggested creating a minimal test app to check if the issue is specific to his main app. If the dropdown worked in the test, the problem was likely in his app; if not, it indicated a version/load issue. Further steps included checking package versions, ensuring JS/CSS was loaded, inspecting elements for click interference, and commonly recent-breaking changes. I encouraged sharing a minimal code snippet where the picker was defined to narrow down the solution further. James was to report on the minimal test app results and package versions to proceed.
